  "novel_mechanics_found": "Level 4's long left-inner shelf can be retracted downward seven bands while still narrow, passing beside the marker before widening. Parked at rows 45-47, it remains below the marker bar; its late growth clips harmlessly against the fixed UI instead of blocking the central actuator. This removes the apparent eight-grow hard cap: cascade only the other three shelves upward and all eleven marker grows reach the diamond. Level 5 couples same-color actuators at different locations: E moves a D marker right while its vertical twin pushes the 9-rail up; C lowers that marker while its twin column creates the rail collision; A separates/recombines a carried D center from an empty diamond socket; and the movable 9-column pushes an otherwise unexplained F block one quantum before that block becomes a hard stop.",
  "narrative": "Recovered the resolver's exact 87-action prefix and observed levels_completed=3 on a fresh reset. On Level 4, I rejected the prior all-shelves-above assumption, retracted the long inner-left shelf below the marker while it was still narrow, and then used the remaining three shelves as a clearance cascade; the eleventh marker grow won Level 4 live at action 120. The mandatory fresh-reset reproduce() gate passed on that exact 120-action sequence with reached_level=4. I continued into Level 5 and decoded its coupled actuator graph, two D marker/socket pairs, the F-wall gap, and the one-quantum F-block stop, but did not find a line that simultaneously clears the E/9 and C/9 couplings before the current-level click budget became the limiting risk. Total accounting is 87 steps in an early diagnostic replay that crashed only while printing the frame, 211 steps in the live winning/exploration run, and 120 steps in the successful gate.",
  "gotchas": [
    "Only ACTION6 was available. Level 4 controls are outer-left (6,48)/(12,48), outer-right (52,48)/(58,48), marker (28,54)/(34,54), long inner-left (6,57)/(12,57), and inner-right (52,57)/(58,57); left retracts/lowers and right grows/raises.",
    "Verified Level 4 extension after the 87-action prefix: long inner-left retract x7; marker grow x7; outer-right raise, outer-left raise, inner-right raise, marker grow; then preserve clearance and repeat the three-shelf upward cascade before each of the last three marker grows. The stored 33-action extension includes three harmless probe no-ops and is gate-verified as written.",
    "The long inner-left shelf must be moved below the marker before any widening. Once the marker bar has grown through its x-range, that shelf cannot be raised back through the bar.",
    "A widening shelf clipped by fixed UI does not necessarily block the marker grow; this is why the parked low shelf can stay at rows 45-47 through grows 9-11.",
    "Level 5 controls at y=57 are 9 at x6/x12, C at x21/x27, E at x36/x42, and A at x52/x57. Each button operates multiple same-color structures, so a locally clear move can be a global no-op because its remote twin is blocked.",
    "Level 5 has two D centers and two four-pixel diamond sockets. Retracting A separates its center marker leftward while leaving an empty diamond behind; growing A recombines them.",
    "Level 5 E can move its marker through the upper F-wall gap at rows 18-20, but C cannot then lower the wide E bar through the lower F segment. Conversely, C can lower a narrow E bar below the wall, but E growth is blocked when its paired 9-rail must move through the extended C column.",
    "The Level 5 9-column can shove the F block from x36-38 to x39-41, but the F block then stops further rightward retraction. That leaves the horizontal 9-rail crossing the C column by one three-cell band.",
    "Every no-op consumes the row-63 click meter, approximately one cell per two clicks; probe coupled actions sparingly."
  ],
